WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.667
A z score describes how far a value is from the mean, measured in standard deviations.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:13.002
We calculate it by subtracting the mean from each value and dividing by the standard deviation.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:21.600
This is a good example of vectorized NumPy code because the same calculation is applied to every element in the array.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:29.215
Standardization is common in statistics and machine learning, especially when variables have different scales.

00:00:29.215 --> 00:00:35.435
In a production machine learning workflow, we usually use a fitted scaler from scikit-learn so the same transformation

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:41.242
learned from the training data can be applied consistently to new data.
